WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.162
NOT negates a Boolean expression In this example
active records are kept

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:10.288
while selected diagnoses are excluded Parentheses
make the target of NOT clear

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.138
the entire IN expression is being negated With
ordinary true and false

00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:20.925
values NOT reverses the result But SQL also has
UNKNOWN If

00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:24.525
an expression is unknown because it depends on NULL
NOT UNKNOWN remains

00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:29.950
UNKNOWN That matters because WHERE keeps only true
rows Use NOT when

00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:33.438
the exclusion rule is clear but be careful when
nullable values are

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.062
involved Sometimes an explicit NULL-safe predicate
communicates the rule more accurately
